        <senderName>NWS San Angelo TX</senderName>
        <headline>Severe Thunderstorm Warning issued August 2 at 2:31PM CDT until August 2 at 3:00PM CDT by NWS San Angelo TX</headline>
        <description>SVRSJT

The National Weather Service in San Angelo has issued a

* Severe Thunderstorm Warning for...
Southeastern Kimble County in west central Texas...

* Until 300 PM CDT.

* At 231 PM CDT, a severe thunderstorm was located 10 miles northwest
of Harper, moving southeast at 5 mph.

HAZARD...60 mph wind gusts.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Expect damage to roofs, siding, and trees.

* This severe thunderstorm will remain over mainly rural areas of
southeastern Kimble County.
</description>
        <instruction>For your protection move to an interior room on the lowest floor of a
building.</instruction>
        <web>http://www.weather.gov</web>
