        <headline>Red Flag Warning issued August 2 at 1:34PM MDT until August 2 at 7:00PM MDT by NWS Grand Junction CO</headline>
        <description>* AFFECTED AREA...In Colorado, Fire Weather Zone 207 Southwest
Colorado Lower Forecast Area. In Utah, Fire Weather Zone 491
Southeast Utah.

* TIMING...Until 7 PM MDT this evening.

* WINDS...Southwest 10 to 20 mph with gusts up to 35 mph.

* RELATIVE HUMIDITY...7 to 12 percent.

* IMPACTS...Any fire that develops will catch and spread
quickly. Outdoor burning is not recommended.
</description>
        <instruction>A Red Flag Warning means that critical fire weather conditions
are either occurring now, or will shortly. A combination of
strong winds, low relative humidity, and warm temperatures can
contribute to extreme fire behavior.</instruction>
        <web>http://www.weather.gov</web>
