        <senderName>NWS Albuquerque NM</senderName>
        <headline>Severe Thunderstorm Warning issued August 2 at 2:33PM MDT until August 2 at 3:00PM MDT by NWS Albuquerque NM</headline>
        <description>SVRABQ

The National Weather Service in Albuquerque has issued a

* Severe Thunderstorm Warning for...
South Central Mora County in northeastern New Mexico...
North Central San Miguel County in northeastern New Mexico...

* Until 300 PM MDT.

* At 233 PM MDT, a severe thunderstorm was located near Watrous, or
19 miles northeast of Las Vegas, moving east at 10 mph.

HAZARD...60 mph wind gusts and quarter size hail.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Hail damage to vehicles is expected. Expect wind
damage to roofs, siding, and trees.

* Locations impacted include...
Watrous, Valmora and Shoemaker.

This includes Interstate 25 between Mile Markers 361 and 365...and
between Mile Markers 366 and 376.
</description>
        <instruction>Seek shelter inside a well-built structure and stay away from
windows. This storm is capable of producing damaging winds and large
hail.

Motorists can expect brief but sudden changes in visibility and
ponding of water on roadways as storms move through the area.</instruction>
