        <headline>Flood Warning issued August 3 at 9:45AM CDT until August 8 at 1:30PM CDT by NWS Quad Cities IA IL</headline>
        <description>...The Flood Warning continues for the following rivers in Iowa...

Wapsipinicon River near De Witt 4S affecting Clinton and Scott
Counties.

* WHAT...Moderate flooding is occurring.

* WHERE...Wapsipinicon River near De Witt 4S.

* WHEN...Until early Friday afternoon.

* IMPACTS...At 12.5 feet, Major Flood Stage. Water affects old U.S.
Highway 61 near the river.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...
- At 9:30 AM CDT Sunday the stage was 11.6 feet.
- Forecast...The river is expected to rise to a crest of 12.4
feet early Wednesday morning. It will then fall below flood
stage early Friday morning.
- Flood stage is 11.0 feet.
</description>
        <instruction>

Caution is urged when walking near riverbanks.

Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood
deaths occur in vehicles.

The next statement will be issued by  Monday morning at 945 AM CDT.</instruction>
